00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,720
What is thermography in?

00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:34,040
Yes, so thermography is basically a test that uses

00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:38,480
an infrared camera to detect different heat patterns

00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:42,720
and blood flow through different body tissues.

00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:46,600
So the camera is going to pick up these, take the image

00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,280
and it's going to pick up these patterns

00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:51,960
and it's basically like a topographical heat map

00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,360
of your body.

00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:57,320
And with this information along with kind of an intake form

00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:01,160
that the patient would fill out about their health history,

00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:05,000
it's sent off to a third party for interpretation.

00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,600
So medical doctors are interpreting this imaging

00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:13,600
and a lot can be determined from these screenings.

00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:16,480
There are many advantages to doing it this way

00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:20,080
for tracking your health care as far as thermography goes.

00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:23,080
What it has to offer is it's no radiation,

00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,920
it's non-invasive.

00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:28,280
It can detect your metabolic function changes

00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:32,320
if it's increasing before any other conventional screening

00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:35,640
such as mammogram, CT, MRIs.

00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:38,480
And then it does go off to those medical doctors

00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,640
who do interpret the report.

00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,000
And they are accredited and certified in reading these reports

00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,480
and putting together something for the patient.

00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:52,320
It can also be a great way of measuring your progress

00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:56,400
in any treatment you're doing conventional or alternative

00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,920
and just monitoring your care that way too.

00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:02,520
So thermography can be used to track acute conditions,

00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:06,680
chronic conditions, and as Ashley talked about

00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,360
can be used in a preventative method as well.

00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:12,840
So if you have chronic pain, if you have fibromyalgia,

00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,640
if you have dental, periodontal inflammation

00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,840
that will be picked up, neuropathy can be picked up,

00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,520
vascular issues, lymphatic congestion,

00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:25,040
all of these things can be picked up in a thermography scan.

00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:27,240
And while it's great for all of these things,

00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:31,360
it's most widely known for breast screening.

00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:35,520
So breast tissue is really sensitive to this imaging.

00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:38,800
And while it's not a diagnostic tool,

00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,400
it's not gonna say, hey, this is breast cancer,

00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:46,280
it can be a great resource for people who maybe have

00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,640
a family history, they're trying to just get their mammograms

00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,520
and they don't wanna be exposed to the radiation

00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,600
and the physical squishing of tissue.

00:02:55,800 --> 00:03:00,000
So we have an image here that gives you an idea

00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,640
of how in relation to a mammogram,

00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:06,720
it takes years before cells have divided

00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:11,720
and multiplied enough to become visible on a mammogram

00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:16,480
where as thermography can pick up these cellular multiplications,

00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,560
these abnormal cellular multiplications,

00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,840
years before it would show up on a mammogram.

00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,640
So it's really great for breast screening.

00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:28,560
So yeah, that image is awesome.

00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:31,760
It is, and it's a great, it's really jaw dropping.

00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:34,600
Yeah, yeah, yeah, for sure.

